1
00:00:00,200 --> 00:00:05,673
[Lecturer] Matrix A ka determinant zero hoga, tabhi non-trivial solution milega.

2
00:00:05,850 --> 00:00:08,355
A real lecture, in two languages at once.

3
00:00:08,450 --> 00:00:10,804
Now imagine it isn't your first language.

4
00:00:10,900 --> 00:00:14,125
The usual answer is the cloud. It stumbles on the mix,

5
00:00:14,250 --> 00:00:15,810
it runs a meter the whole time,

6
00:00:16,850 --> 00:00:18,703
and it assumes the hall has Wi-Fi.

7
00:00:23,250 --> 00:00:25,176
This is Sahaay. Hindi, for help.

8
00:00:26,900 --> 00:00:29,578
Everything you're about to see runs on one laptop.

9
00:00:30,750 --> 00:00:34,000
Whisper writes each sentence down the moment the lecturer pauses.

10
00:00:34,100 --> 00:00:36,934
Then it translates the line, and explains the jargon.

11
00:00:37,050 --> 00:00:39,684
And the words the exam will use come through untouched.

12
00:00:40,700 --> 00:00:44,559
Every caption and translation here is from a real recorded session.

13
00:00:46,900 --> 00:00:49,918
Pick any of twenty-two languages, and the line follows.

14
00:00:54,600 --> 00:00:57,758
Twenty-two scripts, and every one keeps the textbook's words.

15
00:01:02,250 --> 00:01:03,697
Now, switch the network off.

16
00:01:05,300 --> 00:01:06,564
It doesn't even notice.

17
00:01:07,600 --> 00:01:10,579
Nothing is uploaded, because nothing ever needed to be.

18
00:01:13,350 --> 00:01:16,097
On a laptop CPU, Whisper keeps up easily.

19
00:01:16,200 --> 00:01:17,945
Then the glossary model starts too.

20
00:01:19,300 --> 00:01:22,409
The captions start falling behind, and they never catch up.

21
00:01:24,200 --> 00:01:28,735
So the speech encoder moves to the Hexagon NPU, on silicon of its own.

22
00:01:30,250 --> 00:01:33,852
Thirteen and a half milliseconds. Every layer, on the NPU.

23
00:01:34,050 --> 00:01:35,895
Measured on Qualcomm's device farm.

24
00:01:36,350 --> 00:01:39,251
Four hundred tests, on every push, on three platforms.

25
00:01:40,120 --> 00:01:42,169
Offline isn't a promise. It's a test.

26
00:01:42,300 --> 00:01:43,581
One script installs it.

27
00:01:44,200 --> 00:01:45,729
It even runs in your browser.

28
00:01:46,100 --> 00:01:48,015
And it writes your notes when the lecture ends.

29
00:01:50,400 --> 00:01:52,803
Sahaay. The lecture understands you, offline.

30
00:01:53,500 --> 00:01:56,882
Try it in your browser. No install, and nothing uploaded.
